{
  "info": {
    "name": "MainTroll CRUD API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "CRUD API for the MainTroll maintenance database (AWS Lambda `maintroll-crud` + API Gateway HTTP API + RDS MySQL).\n\n## Endpoints\nEvery resource (`users`, `equipment`, `tasks`, `documents`, `alerts`) supports:\n\n| Method | Path | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| GET | `/{resource}` | List rows (`limit`, `offset`, column filters) |\n| GET | `/{resource}/{id}` | Get one row |\n| POST | `/{resource}` | Create a row |\n| PUT / PATCH | `/{resource}/{id}` | Update the fields sent |\n| DELETE | `/{resource}/{id}` | Delete a row |\n\n## Errors\n- `400` invalid value (bad enum, date, limit) or no updatable fields\n- `404` unknown resource or id\n- `409` duplicate key, missing required field, or foreign-key violation\n\n## Setup\nSet the `baseUrl` collection variable (includes the stage, e.g. `.../default`).\n\nRun the folders in order (Users \u2192 Equipment \u2192 Tasks \u2192 Documents \u2192 Alerts): each Create saves its id, which later Creates use as foreign keys."
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "https://wp2a5tdcz5.execute-api.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/default"
    },
    {
      "key": "user_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "task_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "document_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "alert_id",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Users (`musers`)",
      "description": "`/users` - primary key `user_id`.\n\nFields: `name` (required), `email` (required, unique), `role` (required).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List users",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "100",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "offset",
                  "value": "0",
                  "disabled": true
                },
                {
                  "key": "role",
                  "value": "Technician",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns an array of rows. Optional `limit` (max 500), `offset`, and exact-match filters on any column (enable them in the Params tab)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create user",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) pm.collectionVariables.set('user_id', pm.response.json().user_id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Jane Doe\",\n  \"email\": \"jane.doe@example.com\",\n  \"role\": \"Technician\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates a row and returns it (201). `user_id` is generated as a UUID unless you send one. The test script saves it into the `user_id` collection variable."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get users by id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/{{user_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "{{user_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns one row, or 404."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update users by id",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"role\": \"Supervisor\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/{{user_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "{{user_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Partial update: only the fields you send are changed. PUT behaves the same. Returns the updated row."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete users by id",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users/{{user_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "users",
                "{{user_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns 204 on success, 404 if not found. Deleting a row that other rows reference (e.g. equipment with tasks) returns 409."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
